.TH "LANGUAGEMODEL.CONTEXTWINDOW" "3JS" "August 14, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
LanguageModel.contextWindow \- LanguageModel: contextWindow property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]contextWindow\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]LanguageModel\f[R] interface returns the total number of context
window tokens available for this session.
It is set when the session is created and does not change during the
session\(cqs lifetime.
.PP
Compare \f[CR]contextWindow\f[R] against \f[CR]contextUsage\f[R] to
determine how many tokens remain.
Use \f[CR]measureContextUsage()\f[R] to estimate how many tokens a new
prompt would consume before sending it.
.PP
The value is implementation\-specific and varies depending on the model,
device capabilities, and the session\(cqs configuration.
A value of \f[CR]Infinity\f[R] indicates that the user agent does not
impose a hard limit.
.SH VALUE
A number representing the session\(cqs context window capacity in
tokens.
This value may be \f[CR]Infinity\f[R] if the user agent does not impose
a specific limit beyond available memory or JavaScript string
constraints.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Warning when the context is nearly full
The following example uses a function to verify that context is
available before calling \f[CR]LanguageModel.prompt()\f[R].
It first calculates the remaining context and passes that value to
\f[CR]measureContextUsage()\f[R].
If \f[CR]needed\f[R] is less than or equal to \f[CR]remaining\f[R], it
returns \f[CR]true\f[R] and the session continues.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] promptText = \(dqLet me ask you an interesting question...\(dq;
\f[B]const\f[R] session = \f[B]await\f[R] LanguageModel.create();

\f[B]async\f[R] \f[B]function\f[R] contextAvailable(promptText) {
  \f[B]if\f[R] (session.contextWindow === \f[B]Infinity\f[R]) {
    \f[B]return\f[R] \f[B]true\f[R];
  }
  \f[B]const\f[R] remaining = session.contextWindow \- session.contextUsage;
  \f[B]const\f[R] needed = \f[B]await\f[R] session.measureContextUsage(promptText);

  \f[B]return\f[R] needed <= remaining;
}

\f[B]if\f[R] (\f[B]await\f[R] contextAvailable(promptText)) {
  \f[B]const\f[R] response = \f[B]await\f[R] session.prompt(promptText);
  console.log(response);
} \f[B]else\f[R] {
  console.warn(\(dqPrompt skipped: Not enough context window remaining.\(dq);
}
.EE
